WEBVTT

00:06.823 --> 00:08.791
It seems to me
that it'd be more fair...

00:08.958 --> 00:12.325
...if everybody on both basketball teams
was the same height.

00:13.530 --> 00:15.657
That's how it seems to you, huh?

00:16.032 --> 00:17.158
Yeah, like in boxing...

00:17.333 --> 00:20.632
...heavyweights fight heavyweights,
lightweights fight lightweights.

00:21.438 --> 00:22.803
So in your world...

00:22.972 --> 00:25.839
...everybody on a basketball team
would be, say, 6-foot-5...

00:26.042 --> 00:28.738
...and they'd only play other teams
that were 6-foot-5?

00:28.912 --> 00:31.745
Exactly. That way, no one
would have an unfair advantage.

00:31.915 --> 00:35.146
- Huh. That's very interesting.
- You really think so?

00:35.351 --> 00:37.785
No, but it's less likely
to start a fight than:

00:37.954 --> 00:40.252
"That's the dumbest thing
I've ever heard."

00:40.757 --> 00:42.486
And yet you said it anyway.

00:44.761 --> 00:46.251
Listen, I've gotta talk to you.

00:46.463 --> 00:48.363
Okay, "dumb"
was a poor choice of words.

00:48.965 --> 00:51.433
- It's not about that.
- Can it wait till halftime?

00:51.634 --> 00:53.261
No.

00:54.871 --> 00:57.863
- I've gotta go to a funeral this weekend.
- Oh, man, I'm sorry.

00:58.074 --> 01:00.133
- Who died?
- My ex-mother-in-law.

01:00.343 --> 01:02.277
That couldn't wait till halftime?

01:02.479 --> 01:03.810
Charlie.

01:03.980 --> 01:06.972
I'm just saying,
she'll still be dead at halftime.

01:07.884 --> 01:11.183
I was very close to her,
and I wanna pay my respects.

01:11.354 --> 01:13.151
So I'm going to Santa Barbara...

01:13.323 --> 01:16.588
...and I'll be spending the weekend
with my ex-husband.

01:16.793 --> 01:18.693
Oh, okay.

01:23.800 --> 01:25.199
Define "with."

01:25.902 --> 01:28.166
Well, everyone's staying
at his parents' house.

01:28.905 --> 01:30.702
- Do you want me to come with you?
- No.

01:31.174 --> 01:32.801
Great.

01:36.880 --> 01:39.041
- Why not?
- You wanna come?

01:39.249 --> 01:42.184
- Hell, no.
- That's what I figured.

01:43.486 --> 01:46.182
Look, I just wanna be
up-front with you.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.221
I was married to Alex
for eight years...

01:48.391 --> 01:50.655
...and I don't want you
to get the wrong idea.

01:50.827 --> 01:54.388
I wouldn't have had any idea
if you hadn't felt the need to tell me.

01:54.764 --> 01:57.665
Yeah, well, I don't want us
to have secrets from each other.

01:57.867 --> 02:00.335
Oh, I agree.
We definitely should not have secrets.

02:00.503 --> 02:03.904
- Right.
- You know, from this point forward.

02:11.147 --> 02:12.739
What kind of guy is this Alex?

02:12.949 --> 02:14.041
He's a good guy.

02:14.217 --> 02:16.845
We got married too young
and wanted different things.

02:17.053 --> 02:19.419
He wanted something different
than your things?

02:19.589 --> 02:22.023
Because your things are terrific.

02:22.659 --> 02:23.717
Thank you.

02:28.898 --> 02:31.594
- He didn't go gay on you, did he?
- No.

02:32.302 --> 02:33.428
Rats.

02:34.103 --> 02:35.229
Are you jealous?

02:35.438 --> 02:37.872
No, no, of course not.

02:39.242 --> 02:40.368
I mean, maybe a little.

02:40.543 --> 02:42.773
You know, in the sense
that his mother's dead.

03:19.983 --> 03:21.416
I miss you too, honey.

03:21.618 --> 03:23.552
How was the funeral?

03:24.153 --> 03:26.121
Yeah, I guess they're all pretty sad.

03:26.322 --> 03:30.315
Probably why they don't call them
fun-erals. Heh, heh.

03:30.760 --> 03:32.990
Yeah, that was lame.

03:33.696 --> 03:36.062
So where are you now, at the house?

03:36.266 --> 03:37.733
And where is your ex-husband?

03:39.369 --> 03:42.770
And where is his room
in relationship to yours?

03:42.939 --> 03:45.601
Hey, hey, it's got nothing to do
with jealousy.

03:45.775 --> 03:48.107
I just know
based on a lifetime of experience...

03:48.278 --> 03:52.180
...that penises do not observe
a traditional mourning period.

03:53.049 --> 03:56.018
You are not driving my car
until you get a learner's permit.

03:56.219 --> 03:58.278
- Not even in the driveway?
- Not anywhere.

03:58.888 --> 04:00.947
If you have a heart attack,
can I drive you?

04:01.190 --> 04:02.282
No, call an ambulance.

04:02.525 --> 04:04.186
Fine.

04:04.527 --> 04:07.462
If they don't get here in time,
can I have your car?

04:09.465 --> 04:11.899
Hey, hey, hey, there's my posse.

04:12.068 --> 04:14.935
What are we doing tonight, boys?
Think big, it's my treat.

04:16.205 --> 04:19.265
- Drunk?
- Probably.

04:19.475 --> 04:21.875
- Where's Chelsea?
- She had to go out of town.

04:22.078 --> 04:24.603
Oh, so your girlfriend's gone
for a couple of days...

04:24.781 --> 04:26.806
...and now, suddenly,
you have time for us?

04:27.050 --> 04:28.108
Yeah.

04:29.452 --> 04:32.046
Did you ever think
that Jake and I already have plans?

04:32.221 --> 04:34.382
Our lives go on
even when you're not around?

04:34.557 --> 04:37.219
We don't just pop into existence
the moment you need us?

04:37.393 --> 04:38.621
I'm free.

04:39.996 --> 04:42.260
Me too. I'm just making a point.

04:43.299 --> 04:44.425
So, what's it gonna be?

04:44.600 --> 04:45.760
Movie? Bowling?

04:45.935 --> 04:47.402
Putt-putt? Nevada cathouse?

04:47.603 --> 04:49.628
I vote for cathouse.

04:49.839 --> 04:51.466
Do you know what a cathouse is?

04:51.708 --> 04:54.700
Not firsthand,
that's why I voted for it.

04:59.782 --> 05:01.010
A movie would be fine.

05:01.250 --> 05:04.151
All right, movie it is.
What's out that's good?

05:04.354 --> 05:07.414
There's a new pirate movie.
It's rated "Arrrgh."

05:11.494 --> 05:14.327
You guys have no sense of humor.

05:16.232 --> 05:17.756
Can we go to that new theater...

05:17.934 --> 05:20.801
...with the reserved seats
and the jumbo kosher hot dogs?

05:20.970 --> 05:22.164
You just finished dinner.

05:22.372 --> 05:24.533
That doesn't mean I finished eating.

05:26.509 --> 05:27.942
Hey, Charlie.

05:28.144 --> 05:30.112
Wanda. What are you doing here?

05:30.313 --> 05:33.339
I was in the neighborhood,
and I'm drunk and horny.

05:34.884 --> 05:36.818
New plan.

05:46.496 --> 05:47.986
Have I met this one before?

05:48.164 --> 05:51.133
- I doubt it.
- She looks familiar.

05:51.801 --> 05:55.032
Blond, busty and bombed?
Around here, that's familiar.

05:57.273 --> 05:59.833
- I thought Uncle Charlie liked Chelsea.
- He does.

06:00.043 --> 06:01.533
What's he doing with Wanda?

06:02.345 --> 06:03.869
Well, buddy, it's like this:

06:04.047 --> 06:06.242
Uh, despite
his many admirable qualities...

06:06.416 --> 06:09.977
...your Uncle Charlie is,
at heart, a sleazeball.

06:10.186 --> 06:13.644
That's what I figured.
I just wanted a second opinion.

06:13.856 --> 06:16.347
Hang on, I'll grab another bottle.

06:18.528 --> 06:20.723
Broad is part camel.

06:22.065 --> 06:25.000
Except the humps aren't on her back.

06:27.503 --> 06:30.563
Oh, come on,
that was funnier than "Rated 'Arrrgh. "'

06:33.242 --> 06:36.370
I know you're upset. I'll take you
to the movie some other time.

06:36.546 --> 06:38.377
This has nothing
to do with the movie.

06:38.581 --> 06:41.914
- Then what's the problem?
- The problem is you're a sleazeball.

06:42.952 --> 06:44.044
Really? How so?

06:44.720 --> 06:47.587
Oh, please. You're in a committed
relationship with a wonderful woman.

06:47.757 --> 06:50.225
When her back is turned,
you're out gallivanting.

06:50.393 --> 06:52.088
- Gallivanting?
- Screwing around.

06:52.328 --> 06:54.387
Why don't you just say
"screwing around"?

06:55.731 --> 06:59.462
Hey, as we speak, Chelsea is doing
the same thing I'm doing.

06:59.702 --> 07:03.138
Oh, really? She's pouring liquor
down the throat of an inebriated girl?

07:03.372 --> 07:04.862
- Inebriated?
- Drunk.

07:05.041 --> 07:06.872
Jeez, who are you showing off for?

07:09.979 --> 07:13.278
At this moment, Chelsea is in
the same house as her ex-husband.

07:13.483 --> 07:15.576
- Why?
- His mother died.

07:15.785 --> 07:19.346
Oh, my apologies. Clearly,
anything you do at this point is justified.

07:19.555 --> 07:21.716
- No, it's not.
- I was being disingenuous.

07:21.891 --> 07:23.620
- What?
- Sarcastic.

07:23.860 --> 07:26.920
You know, this is why Mom
gets pissed off at you so much.

07:28.898 --> 07:31.093
Look, Charlie, do what you want.

07:31.267 --> 07:33.258
If you can live with yourself,
more power to you.

07:33.469 --> 07:37.098
If I could live with myself, we'd be
having this conversation by telephone.

07:37.740 --> 07:40.231
See, him, I understand.

07:41.744 --> 07:43.439
Charlie, bed, now, come.

07:45.381 --> 07:46.507
Succinct, ain't she?

07:49.185 --> 07:51.449
Does "succinct" mean
what I think it means?

07:52.922 --> 07:54.981
I highly doubt it.

08:00.796 --> 08:02.024
Hello?

08:03.699 --> 08:06.327
Right here, baby.

08:08.804 --> 08:11.637
- Are you okay?
- Yeah, why?

08:13.176 --> 08:14.768
Never mind.

08:14.977 --> 08:18.003
Come on, come on,
let's get you into bed.

08:18.181 --> 08:19.671
Oh, thank you.

08:19.849 --> 08:21.840
Hey, you remember
when we were in Vegas...

08:22.018 --> 08:24.418
...I talked that cute waitress
into joining us?

08:24.921 --> 08:27.856
- Yeah, I do.
- I saw her last week at the Hard Rock.

08:28.057 --> 08:31.026
- No kidding.
- She gained a lot of weight.

08:31.794 --> 08:33.523
- Is that so?
- Yeah, we were lucky.

08:33.696 --> 08:37.132
We nailed her
right before she quit smoking.

08:38.634 --> 08:39.692
Listen, Wanda-

08:39.869 --> 08:41.700
She does smell better though.

08:41.938 --> 08:44.133
- I'm sure, but listen, I-
- Like Fritos.

08:47.076 --> 08:50.944
You know what?
I gotta check on something.

08:51.647 --> 08:53.672
Well, is it okay if I start without you?

08:55.184 --> 08:57.049
Top drawer, nightstand.
Take your pick.

08:58.854 --> 09:02.449
- Ooh.
- Careful. The big one's a flashlight.

09:05.995 --> 09:07.053
That was fast.

09:08.497 --> 09:10.260
I'm guessing.

09:13.536 --> 09:16.994
You're right, I'm a sleazeball.

09:17.206 --> 09:19.231
Don't tell me you actually had
a moral epiphany.

09:19.408 --> 09:22.343
- Uh, "epiphany" means-
- Don't bother.

09:26.048 --> 09:27.879
I don't know what you call it...

09:28.050 --> 09:32.214
...but I've got a gorgeous, willing girl
in my bed, and I'm just not interested.

09:32.421 --> 09:34.412
Maybe you're a gay sleazeball.

09:36.926 --> 09:40.054
I'll tell you what's going on.
You care about Chelsea too much...

09:40.229 --> 09:43.426
...to cheapen your relationship
with a meaningless one-night stand.

09:44.533 --> 09:48.902
You're right, I do care about Chelsea.
I'm crazy about her.

09:49.071 --> 09:50.902
Boy, that sucks.

09:53.876 --> 09:56.276
Hello? Oh, hey, Chelsea.

09:56.445 --> 09:58.106
- We were just-
- Give me that.

09:58.781 --> 10:00.578
Hey, baby, what's going on?

10:01.617 --> 10:02.709
He did?

10:02.885 --> 10:04.512
At his own mother's funeral?

10:04.954 --> 10:07.479
Her ex-husband put the moves on her.

10:07.657 --> 10:08.817
What a sleazeball.

10:11.294 --> 10:13.091
No, no, no, don't blame yourself.

10:13.262 --> 10:15.822
You were right to go to the funeral.

10:16.666 --> 10:18.293
Tonight?

10:19.335 --> 10:22.429
Well, I- I- I'd love to see you tonight.

10:22.605 --> 10:26.632
Isn't it a little late to drive
all the way from Santa Barbara?

10:27.076 --> 10:29.067
Oh, you're already on the road.

10:29.578 --> 10:31.478
Oh, that close?

10:31.947 --> 10:33.847
Wonderful.

10:34.817 --> 10:36.478
Drive safe.

10:36.652 --> 10:39.348
Crap, crap, crap.

10:39.588 --> 10:41.647
Crap, crap, crap.

10:42.091 --> 10:44.582
Remember when I was little,
if someone said "crap"...

10:44.760 --> 10:46.284
...they had to put a dollar in a jar?

10:46.462 --> 10:47.588
I do.

10:47.797 --> 10:49.560
Whatever happened to all that money?

10:52.001 --> 10:56.062
Wanda, don't take this the wrong way,
but you gotta get the hell out of here.

10:56.272 --> 10:57.864
Come on, chop-chop.

11:00.609 --> 11:02.099
Wanda?

11:05.715 --> 11:08.183
Wanda!

11:18.461 --> 11:20.395
Oh, darn.

11:27.370 --> 11:29.930
So the car's a time machine?

11:30.139 --> 11:31.834
Yeah, it's called a DeLorean.

11:32.007 --> 11:33.998
They don't make them anymore.

11:34.510 --> 11:36.842
CHARLIE:
Crap, crap, crap.

11:37.046 --> 11:39.514
- Help. I need help.
- What happened? What's wrong?

11:39.715 --> 11:42.445
Wanda passed out,
and Chelsea's on her way over.

11:42.651 --> 11:44.881
Interesting story about the DeLorean.

11:45.554 --> 11:47.146
It was built by John DeLorean-

11:47.356 --> 11:49.654
Are you not listening?
I've got an emergency here.

11:49.859 --> 11:51.918
A dead girl in your bed
is an emergency.

11:52.094 --> 11:53.789
A passed-out girl is a dinner date.

11:55.798 --> 11:58.426
&lt;i>I don't understand
why it's called Back to the Future.&lt;/i>

11:58.667 --> 12:01.397
They're stuck in the past
and they have to get back...

12:01.604 --> 12:03.367
Home.

12:05.307 --> 12:06.899
Oh, for God's sake, come on.

12:07.076 --> 12:09.943
My girlfriend's on her way
and I've got a half-naked broad.

12:10.179 --> 12:12.170
Half-naked? I'm your man.

12:14.617 --> 12:15.709
Sit down.

12:16.986 --> 12:18.419
Have you tried waking her up?

12:18.621 --> 12:22.318
Well, of course I've tried waking her up.
This is not my first drunk bimbo.

12:22.558 --> 12:24.082
So, what do you expect us to do?

12:24.293 --> 12:26.284
Help me get her dressed,
drive her home.

12:26.495 --> 12:28.588
Enough talk. Let's get to it.

12:29.398 --> 12:32.128
I said, sit down.

12:32.334 --> 12:34.461
- Where does she live?
- I have no idea.

12:34.703 --> 12:38.104
- How am I suppose to drive her home?
- Do I have to think of everything?

12:38.274 --> 12:40.265
- Just help me.
- All right.

12:51.120 --> 12:54.351
- Wow.
- Oh, and I'm a sleazeball?

12:54.590 --> 12:56.615
You're misreading my "wow."

12:56.826 --> 13:00.125
I meant, "Wow, what a predicament."

13:00.796 --> 13:01.854
Yeah, right.

13:02.498 --> 13:04.989
Hold her up, I'll put her dress on.

13:05.234 --> 13:08.431
Okay. She's very fit.

13:09.138 --> 13:11.606
- Hold her arms up.
- Really soft skin.

13:11.774 --> 13:15.301
- Uh-huh.
- Mm. Smells nice too.

13:15.478 --> 13:17.969
Why don't you put
a chloroform-soaked handkerchief...

13:18.147 --> 13:21.048
...over her face and throw her
in the back of your panel van?

13:22.318 --> 13:25.378
Sounds like a waste of chloroform,
doesn't it?

13:28.290 --> 13:31.384
- You get her head, I'll get her feet.
- Why do you get her feet?

13:31.627 --> 13:34.755
- What difference does it make?
- I like feet.

13:35.397 --> 13:37.456
Just get her head.

13:38.334 --> 13:40.029
Okay, on three.

13:40.202 --> 13:42.397
One, two, three.

13:42.571 --> 13:45.199
Oh, oh, oh, goodness.

13:46.642 --> 13:48.007
Slowly, slowly.

13:48.210 --> 13:49.302
Slowly my ass.

13:49.478 --> 13:52.572
- Come on, let's get her out of here.
- Charlie, you're going too- Oh, oof.

13:53.682 --> 13:56.845
ALAN: Goodness gracious, these are real.

14:03.225 --> 14:06.558
Slowly, slowly.

14:08.397 --> 14:11.662
Quickly, quickly.

14:13.936 --> 14:15.665
Hi, baby. Come on in.

14:17.239 --> 14:20.504
Oh, Charlie,
you were so right about Alex.

14:23.078 --> 14:24.739
Alex?

14:24.947 --> 14:26.244
Oh, yeah, Alex.

14:26.415 --> 14:29.043
What a sleazeball.
Can I get you something to drink?

14:29.251 --> 14:31.219
I just want to get in bed
and hold you.

14:31.420 --> 14:32.944
Oh, boy, does that sound good.

14:33.122 --> 14:35.920
- Let me say good night to Jake.
- I'll meet you upstairs.

14:36.091 --> 14:39.720
You know what,
why don't you come say good night too?

14:39.929 --> 14:41.191
Why?

14:41.363 --> 14:42.921
Well, you're my girlfriend...

14:43.098 --> 14:47.125
...and he's my nephew,
and isn't that enough?

14:48.137 --> 14:49.229
Hey, Jake-

14:49.405 --> 14:52.738
Might wanna hang back a sec.
I just ripped off an air biscuit.

14:52.942 --> 14:54.603
- What?
- I farted.

14:54.777 --> 14:57.268
Sorry, I get the fancy words
from my dad.

14:59.114 --> 15:01.207
Chelsea and I
just wanted to say good night.

15:01.417 --> 15:02.975
Okay.

15:03.218 --> 15:05.049
He keeps his feelings bottled up.

15:05.220 --> 15:07.882
Everything else
he shoots into the atmosphere.

15:08.057 --> 15:09.388
- Hi, Chelsea.
Hey, Alan.

15:09.558 --> 15:11.890
- Uh, sorry about your ex-mother-in-law.
- Thank you.

15:12.061 --> 15:14.086
Hey, Jake,
I could really use your help.

15:14.296 --> 15:16.764
- With what?
- I'm taking out the-

15:19.435 --> 15:20.629
I'm taking out the trash.

15:21.270 --> 15:23.261
What are you talking about?

15:23.439 --> 15:25.999
The trash, I'm taking it out...

15:26.241 --> 15:28.471
...and I could use your help
carrying it.

15:28.677 --> 15:31.111
Oh, so now you want my help.

15:31.313 --> 15:32.871
Yes, now I want your help.

15:33.415 --> 15:35.076
What about the 20 bucks
you owe me?

15:37.319 --> 15:38.911
Charlie?

15:42.091 --> 15:43.285
Here.

15:43.459 --> 15:46.189
Is the trash still out
where you can see it?

15:47.129 --> 15:48.460
Never mind.

15:48.631 --> 15:51.395
- Just go help your father.
- Fine.

15:51.600 --> 15:53.693
- Nice seeing you, Chelsea.
- Good night.

15:54.703 --> 15:56.364
I could have said 50, couldn't I?

15:56.538 --> 15:58.631
You could have said a hundred.

15:59.642 --> 16:01.269
Can we please go to bed now?

16:01.477 --> 16:02.944
Beds are for amateurs.

16:03.112 --> 16:04.670
Ooh, Charlie.

16:10.719 --> 16:13.017
What if Jake comes back?

16:13.555 --> 16:15.682
We'll breathe through our mouths.

16:22.164 --> 16:23.825
She really does look familiar.

16:24.033 --> 16:25.694
Terrific. Just don't drop her.

16:25.934 --> 16:28.198
I can't wait
to tell my friends about this.

16:28.437 --> 16:29.870
You're not telling anybody.

16:30.072 --> 16:32.233
What's the point of doing it
if I can't tell?

16:32.941 --> 16:35.535
You've got 20 bucks and a memory,
now shut up.

16:36.879 --> 16:38.813
Okay, we've gotta get her in the car.

16:39.014 --> 16:42.074
- Want me to pull it around?
- I don't want you to pull it around.

16:42.251 --> 16:44.742
Okay, you pull it around,
and I'll stay here with her.

16:45.154 --> 16:47.019
Be very careful.

16:47.956 --> 16:49.981
Come on, let's finish this upstairs.

16:50.159 --> 16:52.093
Move, move, move.

16:54.697 --> 16:56.164
- Chelsea, wait.
- What?

16:57.266 --> 16:59.826
I'm so happy you're back.

17:02.371 --> 17:04.737
- Hey.
- Oh, hey, Alan.

17:04.907 --> 17:07.398
- Is the trash out?
- Almost.

17:07.910 --> 17:09.571
Almost ain't gonna cut it.

17:12.081 --> 17:14.345
Did you at least clean out my room?

17:14.850 --> 17:16.112
Yes, I did.

17:16.351 --> 17:17.784
Good, good.

17:17.986 --> 17:19.248
Okay, well, good night.

17:19.488 --> 17:21.422
Uh, Charlie, can I talk to you for a sec?

17:22.257 --> 17:23.747
- About what?
- Um...

17:23.926 --> 17:25.018
Recycling.

17:25.194 --> 17:29.563
I'm not quite sure what to do
with the big jugs.

17:32.534 --> 17:35.435
Oh, honey, why don't you go up,
and I'll be right there?

17:35.604 --> 17:37.367
- Hurry.
- I will.

17:37.539 --> 17:40.235
First you need to separate
the plastic from the glass.

17:40.442 --> 17:43.275
Then when you get to-
What the hell is your problem?

17:43.779 --> 17:44.871
She's in Jake's room.

17:45.047 --> 17:47.413
- What am I supposed to do?
- I don't know.

17:48.383 --> 17:50.578
Here's my credit card.
Take her to a hotel.

17:50.786 --> 17:52.720
Okay. Chain motel or someplace nicer?

17:53.555 --> 17:56.319
- What?
- You know, room service, ocean view.

17:56.525 --> 17:59.722
That way, when she regains
consciousness, she won't feel so cheap.

17:59.895 --> 18:02.989
Plus, in the nicer places,
you have a free continental breakfast.

18:03.165 --> 18:05.633
Assorted pastries,
freshly squeezed orange juice-

18:05.834 --> 18:07.893
I know what
a continental breakfast is.

18:08.103 --> 18:10.628
- Just get her the hell out of here.
- Okay, fine.

18:12.441 --> 18:14.102
Oh, Charlie.

18:14.276 --> 18:16.403
- What?
- I'm a little low on gas.

18:16.578 --> 18:18.136
- Use the card.
- Right, right.

18:19.348 --> 18:21.839
Charlie.
- What?

18:22.084 --> 18:25.110
- I'm happy you're trying to make it work.
- Go.

18:33.862 --> 18:35.989
What the hell are you doing?

18:36.165 --> 18:38.633
You said I could have a memory.
This is it.

18:39.501 --> 18:41.128
- Give me the phone.
- Oh, good idea.

18:41.303 --> 18:43.066
I can't get us both in the frame.

18:44.807 --> 18:47.002
Can you make it look like
we're talking?

18:47.643 --> 18:51.374
- Forget the picture, bring the car around.
- Shouldn't someone stay with Wanda?

18:51.613 --> 18:53.672
Yeah, but it shouldn't be you.

18:58.120 --> 19:00.213
- Give me the keys.
- You said I could pull it around.

19:00.389 --> 19:03.688
- I changed my mind.
- Okay, I'll tell Mom about Wanda.

19:08.730 --> 19:11.563
One ding, one scratch,
and you're dead.

19:11.733 --> 19:14.361
Dude, mellow out.
You'll give yourself a heart attack.

19:24.980 --> 19:26.971
Hey, look, it's me.

19:29.651 --> 19:31.516
CHARLIE:
I'm glad you came back.

19:32.187 --> 19:36.317
- I don't like it when you're gone.
- I don't like it when I'm gone either.

19:37.759 --> 19:40.489
Oh, here they are.

19:46.401 --> 19:48.528
Funny story.

19:52.507 --> 19:55.840
- Take her head, I'll take her feet.
- Why do you get to take her feet?

19:56.011 --> 19:59.344
Because I'm in charge of this operation,
and I like feet.

20:01.016 --> 20:02.574
Hey.

20:05.687 --> 20:08.679
I guess we don't have to take her
to a hotel, huh?

20:08.857 --> 20:10.347
No, we don't.

20:10.525 --> 20:12.356
- Get in the car.
- Where are we going?

20:12.561 --> 20:15.530
Anywhere we want.
We've got Uncle Charlie's credit card.
